# wasm-pack emits the binary here; commit the JS + .d.ts glue, ignore the built .wasm (mirrors the
# napi crate's `*.node` ignore — SMA-427).
#
# NOTE: `wasm-pack build` CLEANS its --out-dir each run (overwrites .gitignore with a bare `*`,
# DELETES package.json, even with --no-pack). The kernel-ts tasks therefore build into gitignored
# scratch dirs, never into the crate root directly: the `build` task uses `.wasmpack-out` and copies
# only the paigasus_wasm* glue back here (sole crate-dir writer); the `test` task uses its OWN
# `.wasmpack-test-out` and vitest aliases straight at it (no copy), so the two concurrent `moon ci`
# tasks don't race the crate-dir copy. The committed package.json/.gitignore/glue (what the
# `@paigasus/wasm` file: link resolves) are never clobbered. See ts/packages/paigasus-kernel/moon.yml.
*.wasm
.wasmpack-out/
.wasmpack-test-out/
.wasmpack-release-out/

# The release path's UPLOAD staging dir, and the one scratch dir here that is deliberately NOT
# dot-prefixed: `actions/upload-artifact` excludes hidden files by default, so a dot-prefixed path
# uploads NOTHING and fails the job with "No files were found" — measured on prebuild.yml's first
# run with the wasm build in it, after the build step had already reported success. prebuild.yml
# copies the glue and the CRATE-ROOT package.json here, then uploads this directory (SMA-579).
wasm-dist/
